#!/usr/bin/python3
#+
# Builds a TI-5X library module (.ti5l) from a TMC0540 CROM ROM dump
# as published by the Datamath Calculator Museum
# (http://www.datamath.org/Chips/TMC0540.htm) together with the
# corresponding disassembly listing (-PROGRAMS/PGMSUTF8.txt).
#
# The TMC0540 "Solid State Software" module ROM stores plain two-digit
# key codes with a small housekeeping header, which is exactly the
# program format used by the progNN components of .ti5l files:
#
#   addr 0000:       number of programs N (2-digit BCD)
#   addr 0001:       copy-protection flag (ignored when loading)
#   addr 0002 + 2k:  4-digit BCD start address of program k+1,
#                    high pair first (0002..0003 = program 1, etc.)
#   addr 2N + 2:     4-digit BCD end-of-content pointer
#
# Program k of the module becomes bank k of the .ti5l file, so the
# user can select it with "2nd Pgm k" just like on the real hardware.
#
# Invoke as follows:
#
#     mklibfromdump dumpfile listingfile outfile
#
